# Every text file is LF in the index and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git's default on Windows checks out CRLF, and this repository parses its own
# text files in anger: the release scripts read CHANGELOG.md, the corpus gates read fixture
# headers, and the doc gates read markdown. Those parsers are written against `\n`.
#
# That was not theoretical. `bump-version.mjs` matches `/^## Notes toward the first release\n/m`,
# which cannot match across `\r\n`, so `planChangelog` found no promotable section and
# `npm distribution (windows-latest)` failed on `main` -- reproduced locally by converting
# CHANGELOG.md to CRLF, which fails the same test with the same message.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than only `text=auto`: `text=auto` normalises what goes INTO the index (already
# true here -- no tracked file contains CRLF) while leaving checkout to `core.autocrlf`, which is
# the setting that produced the failure. `eol=lf` fixes the checkout too, so the answer does not
# depend on a contributor's local Git config.
#
# Binary files are unaffected: `text=auto` asks Git to detect them, and detected binaries are
# never converted.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Declared explicitly rather than left to detection, because a mis-detected binary that gets
# newline-converted is silently corrupted, and these are the types this repository ships or
# fixtures.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
